WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/features/system/components/status/UpdateAvailableCallout.tsx — a presentational in-page callout shown
  above the System Status chip bar when /system/update-check reports update_available. It surfaces a server-side
  UPGRADE (a new release of the chart/binary) and points the operator at the GitHub release notes so they can
  review what's new before upgrading their deployment. Distinct from the global <NewVersionBanner>.

    Props        : { current?: string, latest?: string, checkedAt?: string }
    Parent       : features/system/pages/SystemStatusPage.tsx — `const { data: updateCheck } = useQuery(['system-status','update-check'])`;
                   `const hasUpdate = updateCheck?.update_available === true`; rendered only when hasUpdate:
                     <UpdateAvailableCallout current={updateCheck?.current} latest={updateCheck?.latest} checkedAt={updateCheck?.checked_at} />
    Title        : "Update available" + (latest ? ` — v${latest}` : "")
    Body         : (current ? `You're running v${current}. ` : "") + "Review the release notes before upgrading your deployment."
                     + (checkedAt ? <span muted> ` · Last checked ${formatDateTime(checkedAt)}` </span> : nothing)
    Link         : "View notes" → https://github.com/ev-dev-labs/teslasync/releases/latest  (target=_blank rel="noopener noreferrer", min-h 36)
    Icons        : lucide Sparkles (lead, cyan-300) + lucide ExternalLink (in the link)
    Chrome       : GlassPanel `border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-500/[0.06]`, role="status", aria-live="polite",
                   data-testid="update-available-callout"
    Data hook    : useDateFormat() → formatDateTime (locale + IANA-timezone aware; web Intl options
                   { year:'numeric', month:'short', day:'numeric', hour:'2-digit', minute:'2-digit' }; "—" for null/invalid)
  i18n           : the web source is "anonymous" — hardcoded English literals (no t() calls). Per the native
                   no-English-literals rule every literal is promoted to a P1/S10 key (table "UpdateAvailableCallout").

