PARITY MAPPING (web → native)
  GlassPanel cyan callout       → card chrome: Color.TS.accent.opacity(0.06) fill + .opacity(0.20) stroke on the
                                  available phase (web bg-cyan-500/[0.06] + border-cyan-400/20); neutral otherwise
  Sparkles / ExternalLink       → SF Symbols "sparkles" (accent) / "arrow.up.right" in the Link pill
  title + ` — v${latest}`       → UpdateAvailableProjection.titleText ("updateAvailable.title" / ".titleVersion")
  `You're running v${current}. `+ review → UpdateAvailableProjection.bodyText (".running" joined with ".reviewNotes")
  ` · Last checked ${fmtDT}`    → UpdateAvailableProjection.lastCheckedText + UpdateAvailableDateFormat.dateTime
                                  (useDateFormat port); rendered as the muted run of a two-tint AttributedString
  "View notes" <a target=_blank>→ SwiftUI Link(destination: releases/latest) + a11y hint "Opens GitHub in your browser"
  role=status / aria-live=polite→ the text block is one combined VoiceOver element; the Link stays a separate actionable element
  useDateFormat (locale+tz)     → UpdateAvailableInput.locale/timeZone threaded into DateFormatter (injected in tests)
  i18n                          → every string via UpdateAvailableStrings (NSLocalizedString table
                                  "UpdateAvailableCallout", web literal as the value: fallback); %@ templates
  telemetry                     → view.opened surface="UpdateAvailableCallout" emitted once on the first apply

STATES (every one renders — no hidden surface)
  loading   → skeleton echo of the callout row (icon + two text lines + button stand-in); web update-check in flight.
  error     → retryable error chrome (P4 leaf addition; the web parent simply withholds the callout on failure).
  upToDate  → friendly "You're running the latest version." with a check-seal glyph (web parent withholds the callout
              when no update; the native surface renders a never-blank state per the prompt's empty contract).
  available → the web callout (sparkles + title + body + muted last-checked + "View notes" link), at parity.
  stale     → header chip + banner + one-shot auto-refresh on the live→stale transition.
  offline   → header chip + banner over the last-known callout; no auto-refresh.

